    {
      "id": "4d3369da-22a9-4615-9cf5-a10a94d9fbfb",
      "name": "Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1700,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## Approved PR Merger\n\nMechanics only; every name and policy comes from the config key.\n\nTwo entry points: the schedule (sweep) and a sub-workflow call from the ingress on an approval event. Human-approved PRs merge when the PR's mergeable state is one of `merge.accept_states` (fallback `merge.require_state`); for any state other than `clean`, every counted check (`ci.checks`) must also have a conclusion in `merge.ok_conclusions`, so a red non-required job cannot hold an approved PR. Dependency-bot PRs merge when `dependabot.auto_merge` is on and the PR is tested (required contexts green, or `dependabot.checks` when the branch declares none); the bot submits the approving review itself. Merge method is `merge.method`, head SHA pinned.\n\nSweep backup for repairs: an open approved pipeline PR that is not clean has its check runs read; each failing counted check (`ci.checks`) becomes a repair item on the intake queue (the sorter dedupes per head SHA + check and applies the attempt cap). A failed merge call goes to the error output and is retried next tick. No model call."
      }
    },
